montage check -- what the probe geometry allows across subjects

1. BIDS *_optodes.tsv, 12 subjects
   optodes compared (those of the shared channels): 25;  max position difference between subjects: 0.000 mm;  distinct z values: [0.0]
   coordsystem: {"NIRSCoordinateSystem":"CapTrak","NIRSCoordinateUnits":"mm","AnatomicalLandmarkCoordinates":{}}
   -> the positions are a flat 2-D TEMPLATE, identical for every subject, with no
      anatomical landmarks. There is no per-subject geometry to register onto, so
      'ROI space' can only mean pooling channels inside a region.

